[Music]  do you have an application with global  reach one with millions or even billions  of users who need highly accurate  real-time information the database that  sits behind your application empowers  your users can dictate your users  experience your ability to grow and your  global resilience  cloud spanner is a strongly consistent  highly scalable relational database that  is fully managed by google cloud so how  is cloud spin are so powerful  well it creates multiple copies or  replicas of your data and stores these  replicas across geographical locations  for enterprises with globally  distributed users a multi-region  configuration is ideal as it protects  against regional failures enables you to  scale to new places and provides faster  reads by having a copy of your database  near your users let's unpack how it  works for multi-region configurations  cloud spanner creates five replicas of  your data and distributes them across  three regions  one region is the leader region which is  responsible for handling rights  the leader logs the right and sends it  to other replicas any right to the  database requires a quorum or agreement  between at least two regions  this ensures that if a region fails  there are at least two regions that can  form a quorum with full up-to-date  copies of your data so your database can  continue to be available without any  data loss so what happens if the leader  region fails  cloud spanner is built to be resilient  and moves the leader to another region  the new leader region and the other  available region form the quorum this  means the database continues to be  available your application might see  slightly higher latencies during the  later movement but won't experience any  downtime to scale your application  across the world you can use read-only  regions close to your users reads and  cloud spanner will by default read the  latest data these are called strong  reads and are served by a replica  closest to the user  if the read is in a different region  from the leader the replica may have to  communicate with the leader to know  whether it has the latest data and this  can increase latency to get faster reads  you can use stale reads stale reads are  done at a time stamp in the past  for example 15 seconds in the past and  are useful if you can tolerate slightly  older data businesses around the world  are powering their users with cloud  spanner  a multi-region configuration gives you  the peace of mind that you have high  availability low latency and resilience  against regional failures  to find out more check out the cloud  spanner website  [Music]  you

